{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HaaF4H9bVgfNpNKpY3vjqr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n     2\t\n     3\t```\n     4\tKnown plaintext: \"Nice work decoding this warmup! To solve, submit this exact answer to the Game Master: a-b-c-NN\"\n     5\t word lengths: 4 4 8 4 6! 2 5, 6 4 5 6 2 3 4 6: slug   (exactly one \"!\", one \",\", one \":\")\n     6\t crib letters cover all but f j q y z; slug is ALWAYS lowercase -> lowercase case-losing decodes before submit\n     7\tSTEP 1 - lib first: python3 -c \"from lib import decode,warmups_codecs as w;t=open('blob.txt').read();\n     8\t  print(decode.decode_chunk(t)); print([n for n,e,d in w.CANDIDATES if d and w.SLUG.search(w.safe(d,t.strip()) or '')])\"\n     9\tSTEP 2 - charset fingerprint (python: sorted(set(t)), len(t), len(t)/110):\n    10\t [01] 8/7-groups .................. binary (D4); 4-groups -> nibbles->hex; 5-groups -> Bacon/Baudot; 0-blocks -> Chuck Norris\n    11\t [0-7] 3-digit ................... octal (D6);   [0-9] 32-126 tokens -> decimal (D5); 1-26 dashed -> A1Z26\n    12\t ONE long digit run, no spaces .... whole text as a big integer (to_bytes big/little); 4-10 digit tokens -> u16/u32 words\n    13\t digit pairs 1-5 -> Polybius/tap code (. or x knocks too);  runs of 2-9 repeats -> multitap (44 33 555); 2-9 singles -> T9\n    14\t [0-9a-f] even, x2 ................ hex (D3); c1-e9/81-a9 + 40 -> EBCDIC cp037\n    15\t hex x4 starting fffe (D19 LE 4e00) / feff (D20 BE 004e), 00 every 2nd byte = UTF-16: .decode('utf-16') takes EITHER BOM;\n    16\t   fffe0000/0000feff -> UTF-32; NULs in a non-LE/BE 4-byte pattern -> middle-endian; d8xx dcxx -> surrogates, then NFKC;\n    17\t   pairs/quads swapped -> byte-swap words; base64 with AG/AA rhythm -> b64 then utf-16-le; LSB-first bits\n    18\t . - only (+ / or 3 spaces) ....... Morse (D16: output only 0-9A-F -> hex layer; digits -> char codes); 1/111 runs -> timing\n    19\t a/b (A/B) in 5s .................. Baconian (D17: all groups start `a` -> values 0-15 = HEX nibbles, 2 per byte);\n    20\t                                    values up to 25 -> letters; odd casing in cover text -> Bacon via case\n    21\t ANY 16-symbol output (0-9A-F, a-p only, 16 words) after a carrier = hex nibbles -> fromhex (D16, D17);\n    22\t   unknown 16 tokens -> map them by the crib hex `4e 69 63 65 20 77 6f 72 6b`. lib: twosym/bin4/aphex/tern/radix_dec\n    23\t 2-symbol groups of width 5/6 with values >15 -> base32/base64 INDEX;  ䷀.. hexagrams -> base64;  only space/TAB -> bits\n    24\t dotted quads/#RRGGBB/4e69:6365 -> IPv4/colour/IPv6 bytes; b64-ish won't decode -> undo rev/rot13 1st (U4fV=rot13 H4sI)\n    25\t %XX .............................. URL (D7);  &#..; -> HTML (D8);  \\uXXXX -> JSON (D9);  \\xNN -> C escape\n    26\t U+004E U+0069 (D25, 7 B/char) / %uXXXX / \\U0000XXXX / \\u{4E} -> chr(int(h,16)); mixed prefixes -> one alternation tokenizer\n    27\t   LATIN SMALL LETTER I / \\N{..} -> unicodedata.lookup;  =XX / soft \"=\\n\" -> quoted-printable;  =?UTF-8?B?..?= -> MIME\n    28\t N:c,N:c, ... digits:payload, ..... NETSTRINGS (D24, every len 1): count-cursor parse, never split(','); payload `,`/`:`\n    29\t   are data (1:,, 1::,). No comma -> bencode (l..e, i..e)/sexp; tag ,#!~^]} -> tnetstring; $len CRLF -> RESP; hex len -> chunked\n    30\t A-Z2-7 (=) ....................... base32 (D10);  0-9A-V -> base32hex;  ybndrfg8.. -> z-base-32;  no ILOU -> Crockford\n    31\t A-Za-z0-9+/ (=), len%4==0 ........ base64 (D1); H4sI = GZIP inside (D21: base64 -d | gzip -dc); eN = ZLIB 78da (D22:\n    32\t   zlib.decompress(b64decode(t)); eJ/eF/eA other levels; zlib = (b0<<8|b1)%31==0, not just 0x78; no magic -> wbits=-15);\n    33\t   Qlpo bz2, /Td6WFo xz, KLUv/ zstd, UEsDB zip, N3q8 7z, U2FsdGVkX1 openssl, .eJ flask cookie, eyJ JWT -> never score bytes\n    34\t A-Za-z0-9-_ no = ................. base64url (D11);  [0-9A-Za-z] only, no pad -> base62 (x1.34) / base36 one case (x1.55)\n    35\t no 0 O I l + / = -> base58 (x1.37);  0-9A-Z plus space $%*+-./: -> base45 (x1.5)\n    36\t <~ ... ~> around ! .. u ......... ASCII85 (D23): a85decode(t,adobe=True); no <~ -> a85decode (z = 4 NULs);\n    37\t   RFC1924 set (no quotes , . / : [ \\ ]) -> b85decode; .-:+=^!/*?&<>()[]{}@%$# -> Z85; xbtoa Begin -> btoa\n    38\t ~all printable, no ' - \\ ......... basE91 (x1.23);  ! .. } minus \" ` -> base92;  no chunk structure -> bignum radix\n    39\t begin 644 / lines start M or h ... uuencode / xxencode;  xn-- labels -> punycode/IDNA;  ADFGX(V) only -> ADFGVX (key: title word + crib);  A C\n    40\tNON-ASCII: U+2800-28FF ⠝⠊⠉⠑ ...... Braille (⠼ = number sign)\n    41\t fullwidth Ｎｉｃｅ / math 𝐍𝐢𝐜𝐞 / ⓝ -> NFKC;  ɐ q ɔ p ǝ ɟ ƃ ɥ ᴉ ʞ ɯ ɹ ʇ ʌ ʍ ʎ -> upside-down (from_upside_down\n    42\t CJK U+7Cxx + spaces -> ROT8000; dense CJK/Hangul -> base65536/2048; emoji 1/byte -> base100; CJK U+xx00 -> swap bytes\n    43\t zero-width U+200B/C/D/2060/FEFF -> bits; U+E00xx tags -> cp-0xE0000; FE00../E0100.. selectors -> bytes; one block with\n    44\t   ord-ord(crib) constant -> code-point offset; runes/Greek/Cyrillic, lengths kept -> crib map; Cyrillic look-alikes -> homoglyph\n    45\tSAME LENGTH, LETTERS ONLY CHANGE (word lengths 4 4 8 4 6! ... kept):\n    46\t best rot-N English -> Caesar (D2 rot13, D14 +7); digits also +5 -> ROT18/ROT5;  mirror a<->z -> Atbash (D13)\n    47\t crib c-p constant ratio .......... affine (lib _fit_affine); constant per position mod k -> Vigenere key = (c-p)\n    48\t crib c+p periodic -> Beaufort (primer then plaintext -> autokey);  crib map consistent, not affine -> keyword subst\n    49\t neighbour keys (Muvr eptl) ....... QWERTY shift;  ;,.' in words -> Dvorak;  ALL printables shift -> ROT47 (D15)/ROT8000\n    50\tSAME CHARACTER MULTISET (one ! , :, slug digits intact) = TRANSPOSITION (D12 reverse, D18 rail 3 = prompt number):\n    51\t w.rail_solve | redefence | w.col_solve | route/Caesar box | sk