g).\"},\n {\"id\":\"unseparated-token-bf\",\"concept\":\"BF token dialects with UNKNOWN or UNSEPARATED tokens: new word triads paired like Ook (Meep. Meep? Meep!), emoji BF, CamelCase/no-space words, multi-char glyph units\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Direct knob of D27 (same program, other spelling). bfd_dec's crib solver assumes separable tokens; add a segmenter: grapheme clusters (emoji with ZWJ/VS16 kept whole), [A-Z][a-z]* runs, word+[.?!] marks, fixed-width k-char units (k=2..8) when the text has no separators. If <= 3 distinct units, try Ook-style PAIRING (9 ordered pairs -> 8 commands; pair from offset 0 and 1). Then assign units/pairs to +-<>[].,: the GM's delta program has exactly three used commands with run structure (+ runs, - runs, single '.' between runs) -> the unit that never repeats twice in a row is '.', the two run units are +/- (decide by the crib: first output must be 'N' = 78 from cell 0). Run bf_dec, slug gate. Fixtures: Meep/Hmm/Eek triads, emoji 3-unit and 8-unit maps without spaces, CamelCase 'MooMooMoo', 2-char units 'aZaZbY'; decoys: Morse, plain prose, base64.\"},\n {\"id\":\"brain-flak\",\"concept\":\"Brain-Flak ((), [], {}, <> only; two stacks) printing the sentence\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Brain' sibling of BF/Ook. brainflak_dec(t): whole text in '()[]{}<>' + whitespace, balanced; nilads () = 1, [] = stack height, {} = pop, <> = toggle stacks; monads (X) = push value of X (and evaluate to it), [X] = negative of X, {X} = loop while top != 0, <X> = evaluate X, return 0. Output = final active stack from TOP to bottom as chr (the -A ASCII flag); also try bottom-to-top and decimal numbers. Step cap 10^7. Fixtures: the standard 'push each char as ((()()()...){}...)' generator (repeated doubling), a loop-based generator; decoys: balanced bracket soup from JSON/Lisp (must fail the slug gate).\"},\n {\"id\":\"chicken-animal-esolangs\",\"concept\":\"animal-word esolangs: Chicken (opcode = number of 'chicken' words per line), Hodor, Meow-likes, other one-word languages\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Monkey Business' -> another animal day is a plausible pun path (COW and Pikalang are built in bfd_dec). Chicken VM: stack[0] = pointer to stack, stack[1] = user input, program = list of line word-counts; ops 0 axe(exit) 1 chicken(push 'chicken') 2 add 3 fox(sub) 4 rooster(mul) 5 compare 6 pick(load; next op is the source flag) 7 peck(store) 8 fr(jump if) 9 BBQ(top -> '&#N;' HTML entity char) 10+ push n-10; output = top of stack at exit (often a string of &#N; entities -> html.unescape). Hodor: Hodor/hodor/HODOR/Hodor? variants map to BF (treat as row-194 unknown map). Fixtures: Chicken program printing the sentence via BBQ, a 'chicken' line count generator; decoys: prose with repeated words.\"},\n {\"id\":\"spoon-prefix-code-bf\",\"concept\":\"Spoon / prefix-code BF (1=+ 000=- 010=> 011=< 00100=[ 0011=] 001010=. 0010110=,) and BF packed as bits in hex/base64\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Binary spelling of BF without fixed group width (Binaryfuck 3-bit is built). spoon_dec(t): strip whitespace, require [01]+, greedy prefix-code parse (also the inverted polarity and the 00101110 debug / 00101111 exit codes), then bf_dec. Also unpack hex/base64 bytes to bits MSB- and LSB-first and try the same. Fixtures: Spoon of the delta program, packed into bytes then hex/base64; decoys: 8-bit binary ASCII (D4 must still win via slug gate order).\"},\n {\"id\":\"boolfuck-bitlevel-bf\",\"concept\":\"bit-level BF: Boolfuck (+ flips bit, ; outputs bit, bytes LSB-first), Smallfuck, Bitfuck\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"boolfuck_dec(t): alphabet '+,;<>[]' (no '-' or '.'); bit tape, '+' flips, ';' appends the current bit to the output bit stream, ',' reads 0; bytes assembled LSB-first (also try MSB-first) -> printable + slug gate; step cap. Smallfuck ('*' flips, no output: skip). Fixtures: the standard Boolfuck text generator output for the sentence; decoys: BF programs (no ';').\"},\n {\"id\":\"headsecks-wordfuck-bf\",\"concept\":\"BF by arithmetic on characters/words: Headsecks (ord % 8 -> command), Wordfuck (word length -> command), TinyBF (+ > | =), Brainloller-as-text\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cover-text spellings of BF. Headsecks: command = ord(c) % 8 over '+-<>.,[]' order per spec (try the 8 rotations/orders only via the crib: first output char 'N'). Wordfuck: word length (or length % 8) -> command. TinyBF: '+' inc/dec by direction, '>' move by direction, '=' flips direction, '|' loop; output via '==' pattern per spec. High false-positive risk -> accept ONLY when the program output passes the slug gate. Fixtures each; decoys: English prose, base64 (must not produce a slug).\"},\n {\"id\":\"print-statement-esolangs\",\"concept\":\"print-statement / prose languages: LOLCODE (VISIBLE), ArnoldC (TALK TO THE HAND), INTERCAL (PLEASE READ OUT, Turing-Text-Model), Rockstar (poetic literals, Say), Emojicode\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Chatty'/'say' re-read. Extract string literals from keyword frames (VISIBLE \\\"..\\\", TALK TO THE HAND \\\"..\\\", Say \\\"..\\\", 🗨 / 😀 🔤..🔤) and join; LOLCODE ':)' newline escapes. INTERCAL: ',1 SUB #n <- #v' arrays + READ OUT ,1 -> Turing Text Model decode (each value v: prev_bits - v mod 256, then reverse the 8 bits of the result to get the char). Rockstar poetic number literals: each word's length mod 10 = a digit ('.' = decimal point) -> numbers -> chr, 'Say/Shout/Whisper X'. Fixtures each printing the sentence; decoys: plain English with 'say'.\"},\n {\"id\":\"unlambda-rewrite-langs\",\"concept\":\"combinator / rewriting languages: Unlambda (`.x print, r newline), Lazy K / Iota, Thue (a::=b), /// (slashes)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Unlambda: tokenise ` s k i v d c e r .x ?x |; a small applicative evaluator (step cap) -- the usual generated program is ``` ``...`.N`.i`.c ... i ``` where output order = application order; fast path: if the program is a left-spine of `.x applications, read the .x chars in order. Thue: rules 'lhs::=rhs' until '::=', then the initial string; apply rules (deterministic first-match) with '~' output; ///: /pattern/replacement/ rewrite loop with '\\\\\\\\' escapes, output = remaining text. Step caps everywhere. Fixtures each; decoys: shell/Markdown with backticks and slashes.\"},\n]\n# insert new p1 gaps after the p1 notes, p2 after built p1 prebuilds, p3 near end\norder=[g['id'] for g in gaps]\ndef ins_after(after_id, items):\n    i=[g['id'] for g in gaps].index(after_id)+1\n    for it in reversed(items): gaps.insert(i,it)\nN={g['id']:g for g in new}\nins_after('byte-family-mastery-cost',[N[k] for k in ('program-output-redecode','unseparated-token-bf','brain-flak','chicken-animal-esolangs')])\nins_after('whitespace-language',[N[k] for k in ('spoon-prefix-code-bf','boolfuck-bitlevel-bf','headsecks-wordfuck-bf','print-statement-esolangs')])\nins_after('malbolge',[N['unlambda-rewrite-langs']])\nfor g in new: assert g['id'] not in ids\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+'\\n]\\n'\njson.loads(body)\ns=s[:a]+body+s[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('warmups:'+g['id'],{}).get('ok') or st.get('warmups:'+g['id'],{}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend),pend)\nEOF","description":"Rewrite readiness gaps JSON with new gaps"}}}
